nodecode-yandex-calendar is a rewrite of akinfold's akinfold/hermes-yandex-calendar:
https://github.com/akinfold/hermes-yandex-calendar
commit cad2a6b8e1cad82753b9f57d4f388645210702a0
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Roman Akinfeev (LICENSE)

The Python plugin registered seven tools with the Hermes agent; this rewrite
registers the same seven names with a Nodecode cell, and reimplements the CalDAV
client, the iCalendar reading and writing, and the XML reading in Common Lisp on
the cell's own HTTP seam, so no Python and no package of the original is
bundled. The tool arguments moved from hand-written JSON Schemas to contract
declarations, which derive both the schema the model reads and the record the
body reads. The settings became the cell's `yandex_calendar` section instead of
environment variables, and `actions` is decided at start by registering only the
allowed tools, as the plugin decided it at registration time. Left out: the
original's time-zone resolution through Python's zoneinfo, which needs a
time-zone database — a `TZID` time is read as that local time here and written
back verbatim while it is unchanged; the original's Expat version floor, which
only mattered to pyexpat; and its `YANDEX_CALENDAR_CALENDARS` environment
variable, whose ordered allow-list is the section's `calendars` member.
